Revision history for Unblock-WebSocket

0.01  unreleased

    - Begin standalone platform- and event-loop-neutral WebSocket engine.
    - Add portable client and server byte-stream protocol engines.
    - Add framing, masking, fragmentation, UTF-8, Ping/Pong, and Close handling.
    - Add Uniform::HTTP handshake support for HTTP/1.1 Upgrade and HTTP/2 or
      HTTP/3 Extended CONNECT.
    - Define a private versioned native-adapter ABI for zero-copy-capable transports.
    - Add a vendored bq_websocket native engine with portable secure random masking.
    - Add Linux, macOS, and Windows CI for the native core.
    - Use the native engine by default behind the public client/server API while
      retaining the Perl engine as a differential reference backend.
    - Port RFC 6455 parser vectors, UTF-8 edge cases, protocol-error mappings,
      and close lifecycle regressions into standalone in-memory tests.
    - Add callback-order and handshake rejection/subprotocol regression coverage.
    - Preserve RFC 3629 Unicode noncharacters in the portable UTF-8 path while
      still rejecting surrogates and values above U+10FFFF.
    - Correct invalid UTF-8 Close reasons to use Close 1007 in the Perl backend.
    - Add native rejected-Close memory-lifetime regressions for ownership safety.
    - Add a repository-only Autobahn client/server author harness using blocking
      socket adapters around the public byte API.
    - Keep repository infrastructure and author tests out of the CPAN manifest.
    - Fix generated client-handshake nonce validation and add a regression for
      the real secure-random path.
